  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. Here N≤50N \\le 50N≤50 and sum of N≤500N \\le 500N≤500.**\n\nAn array AAA is called sortable if it can be sorted in **strictly ascending order** with the use of the following operation any number of times:\n\n\nChoose index iii and a **positive integer** XXX, and then update AiA_iAi​ to Aimod  XA_i \\mod XAi​modX.\nStrictly ascending order means that A1&lt;A2&lt;…&lt;A∣A∣A_1 &lt; A_2 &lt; \\ldots &lt; A_{|A|}A1​&lt;A2​&lt;…&lt;A∣A∣​.\n\nYour task is to find the number of sortable subarrays of AAA, i.e. find how many pairs (L,R)(L, R)(L,R) exist such that 1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N and [AL,AL+1,…,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,…,AR​] is sortable.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of sortable subarrays of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤501 \\le N \\le 501≤N≤50",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500500500."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
